# Scissor (scissor-app)

macOS-first **Electron** desktop app: local video dedupe, timeline cut/export, and ffmpeg-based transforms (speed/hue/stickers/etc.). Heavy work stays in the **main** process; UI is **React 18** + **TypeScript strict**.

## Layout

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `src/main/` | Main process: `ipcMain`, dialogs, `ffmpeg-utils`, `dedupe`, `export-timeline` |
| `src/preload/` | `contextBridge` → `window.scissor` |
| `src/renderer/` | Vite + React UI (`src/renderer/index.html` entry) |
| `src/shared/types.ts` | Types shared by main / preload / renderer |
| `resources/` | Bundled assets (e.g. logos); packaged path vs dev differs in main |
| `out/` | **Build output — never edit by hand.** Change `src/` and run `npm run build` |

## Commands

- Dev: `npm run dev` (electron-vite)
- Build: `npm run build`
- Run packaged main: `npm start` → loads `out/main/index.js` per `package.json`

## Runtime deps

Uses **system** `ffmpeg` / `ffprobe` (PATH / Homebrew). Main resolves binaries via `resolveBinariesSync()` in `ffmpeg-utils.ts`.
